--TEST--
`Core\Socket::upgrade`'s entry is a sink, so a path that came from outside the program cannot select what a connection runs — ADR 0083 § 2, ADR 0097 § 2
--ARGS--
sockets/chat.nvs
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The entry's content becomes the instruction "execute this file", which is
// ADR 0088 § 1's definition of a sink, and ADR 0097 § 2 is the same rule
// written for the server: a filesystem path is never *constructed* at request
// time, only selected from a set enumerated before the request arrived. An
// upgrade is a request-time call, so a word that arrived from outside is shut
// out here even though it names a file that exists.
foreach (Core\Cli::arguments() as tainted string $word) {
    Core\Socket::upgrade($word);
    echo "unreachable\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:9:26
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
